  "id": "COMPOUND:31303 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between 32,33-dihydro-31-hydroxymanzamine A and CD70 antigen, mediated through DMS-79 and Cinnamtannin A2. These compounds appear to act as intermediaries, with 32,33-dihydro-31-hydroxymanzamine A targeting DMS-79, which in turn targets CD70 antigen. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust connection, suggesting that the mechanism involves a series of target engagement steps. The shared involvement of DMS-79 in multiple pathways reinforces the idea of a common functional pathway, while the distinct targets of Cinnamtannin A2 and the complex structure of the third pathway highlight the diversity of interactions. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that 32,33-dihydro-31-hydroxymanzamine A may exert its biological effects through a multi-step process involving these compounds, potentially modulating CD70 antigen activity in a broader biological context.",
